  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added the new names next to the old ones, because a straight rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which consume `OrderPlaced`. ARCH-4 says changes must be additive and renames go through deprecation. All 39 tests pass.\n\nIn `src/core/events.ts`, `OrderPlaced` now carries both names with identical values:\n- **`createdAt`:** the new name for `placedAt`.\n- **`amountCents`:** the new name for `totalCents`.\n- **`placedAt` and `totalCents`:** kept and marked `@deprecated`.\n\n`schemaVersion` is still 3. A bump could trip consumers that check the version, and an additive change doesn't need one. If you want a bump, ask billing-service and analytics-ingest first.\n\nI updated the event assertions in `test/app.test.ts` to cover the new fields.\n\nI left the `GET /orders/{id}` response (`placedAt`, `totalCents`) alone, because web-storefront uses it and ARCH-8 requires it to stay compatible. You only asked about the event.\n\nRemoving the old fields needs a follow-up once both consumers have moved to the new names. I can't tell from this repo whether they have.",
